## 2026-08-05 - STEP 2 (hash toolkit)
- what: seedable tabulation hashing, k independent functions. why: the e/d promise rests on fair spreading - tested, not assumed. concept: uniform hashing + independence. next: Bloom warm-up. Commit 7b1ca0a, CI 17s. Lesson kept for the page: tests caught a Python 3.11 seeding TypeError before push.

## 2026-08-06 - STEP 3 (Bloom warm-up)
- what: bit-array membership sketch on the step-2 hash family. why: first taste of one-sided controlled error - can say 'maybe', never a false 'no'. concept: probabilistic membership, analytic FPR (Bloom CACM 1970). next: sizing calculator (n + target FPR -> m,k). Commit 3208dae, CI 12s.

## 2026-08-08 - STEPS 4+5 (backlog reconcile after 2-day Surface outage)
- step 4: what: sizing calculator n+target FPR -> (m,k). why: first hands-on 'buy accuracy with memory' (~1.44 bits/item per halving of error). lesson kept for the page: textbook k-rounding broke the promise (analytic 0.01004 > 0.01); fixed with best-k + m-bump so the maths delivers exactly. Commit ad72e7c.
- step 5: what: CMS skeleton - depth x width counters on the step-2 hash family. why: the hero begins; concept: never-undercount invariant (collisions only inflate). gate: every counter >= true count across a 10k Zipfian stream. Commit e2df3f4, CI 19s. next: min-query + eps/delta sizing (step 6, first green tag).
- ops note: 07-Aug bridge outage handled cleanly - chain armed first, build done in container, ship parked, page never claimed DONE ahead of CI. Two-step catch-up shipped as two separate commits to keep per-step history honest.

## 2026-08-09 - STEP 6 (CMS min-query + ε/δ sizing) + FIRST CHECKPOINT TAG
- what: query() = min of row counters (the tightest overestimate) + size_cms(ε,δ) → (width=⌈e/ε⌉, depth=⌈ln(1/δ)⌉). why: this completes the hero's core guarantee — now we can SIZE a sketch for a target accuracy AND QUERY it, and the additive error bound holds. concept: the ε·N additive error bound + min-estimator. next: step 7, memory accounting + serialize/deserialize.
- gate design note: the ε/δ guarantee is PER-KEY (for any fixed key x, P(error > ε·N) ≤ δ over hash randomness), not simultaneous across all keys. Initial test checked all keys per trial and saw 12.5% failure rate (union bound inflates it). Redesigned: 300 seeds, per-key failure rate checked on top-10 heavy hitters individually, each ≤ 3·δ margin. Passes cleanly.
- tag: green-sketchflow-1 cut at commit 1e6bae1 — 7 green steps (0–6), the first checkpoint per Rule 6.
- Commit 1e6bae1, CI 34s.

## 2026-08-10 - STEP 7 (CMS memory accounting + serialize/deserialize)
- what: bytes_used() measures real Python memory via recursive sys.getsizeof; to_bytes()/from_bytes() for compact binary round-trip. why: honest memory measurement matters — Python list-of-lists overhead is ~4× the packed minimum; comparing sketch vs exact-dict memory is meaningless without measuring what the interpreter actually allocated. concept: measuring real memory footprint honestly; serialization as the bridge between in-memory and on-disk. next: step 8, CMS inner-product / join-size estimate between two sketches.
- gate design note: bytes_used walks outer list + each inner list + every int cell with sys.getsizeof; test independently recomputes the same walk and asserts equality. Serialization uses struct.pack little-endian: 24-byte header (width u32 + depth u32 + seed i64 + total u64) then row-major uint64 counters. from_bytes validates header length and total blob size; corrupt inputs raise ValueError. 10 new tests, 38 total green.
- Commit 9912643, CI 35s.

## 2026-08-12 - STEP 8 (CMS inner-product / join-size estimate)
- what: inner_product(other) estimates the dot product of two frequency vectors via min of row-wise dot products. why: sketches are linear — two streams counted independently with the same hashes can be compared without seeing the raw data; this is the join-size estimator (how many matching pairs?). concept: linear sketches compose; sketches as vectors; join-size estimation. next: step 9, conservative-update CMS (increment only minimum cells to reduce overestimation).
- gate design note: error bound ε·‖a‖₁·‖b‖₁ tested across 200 hash seeds on two 5k Zipfian streams; empirical violation rate ≤ 3·δ margin. Also verified: never undercounts (est ≥ true), symmetric, self-join ≈ L2² (within 5% on low-collision setup), disjoint universes bounded, weighted adds correct, dimension/seed mismatches rejected. 11 new tests, 49 total green.
- reconciliation note: code was built by a prior run but left uncommitted in the working tree (orphaned build). Verified tests pass, committed and pushed as today's step.
- Commit 51397cc, CI 52s.
